Done, in "[PATCH 0/5] Base lab-process-mail work on LAB_BASE_BRANCH"
[1]. Patch 5 is the new one. It reads LAB_BASE_BRANCH, which defaults
to trunk(). It uses that base to rebase unmerged work, to create the
pass workspace, and to select the work revset. It also passes the base
to the agent as "Your base is <revset>.", so the prompt's rebase and
new-change steps follow it. Series still apply to trunk, and the
prompt says to treat a non-trunk base as a prerequisite when
formatting.

I tested one case you will hit often: b/dev being rebuilt upstream.
Work built on the old b/dev moves to the new head, and the old b/dev
commits are dropped rather than copied along. All 14 tests pass under
kyua, including the new ones.

lab-process-mail only exists on b/dev, so patches 1-4 are its four
commits as they stand there, which are patches 1-4 of "[PATCH 0/6]
Answer the inbox with lab-process-mail" [2]. They are included only
for context.

